purpose:
• overseeing financial reporting;
• assessing internal controls, including fraud control by a process of reporting and
dialogue with management, internal and external auditors; and
• evaluating the audit process;

responsibilities:
resolve any disagreements between management and the external auditor regarding financial reporting;
• approve proposed auditing fees for external auditors;
• seek independent, professional advice to assist it to carry out its responsibilities;
• seek any information it requires from employees, all of whom are expected to cooperate
with the committee's requests, or external parties; and
• meet with company officers, external auditors, or outside counsel, as necessary.
